            <ArticleTitle>Targeting Interleukin-5 in Patients With Severe Eosinophilic Asthma: A Clinical Review.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>196-201</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Interleukin-5 (IL-5) is known to play a major role in the growth, differentiation, recruitment, and activation of eosinophils. The authors review the efficacy and safety of two IL-5-targeting agents used in the treatment of eosinophilic asthma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
